It is not possible for us to back up the games because none of the regular
players has the correct permission to the games directory.
On occasion, our system administrator will replace a game lost due to a
segmentation fault from the backup tapes, this means replaying a significant
portion.  My two games, Gandalf and Rex Morgan, were well behaved and I 
did not suffer any errors of any sort, so they are definitely pure wins. 
The player in 8th place on this list was the first to be 
successful, and he exploited the game bug that allowed infinite wishes.
All the other games were at Patchlevel 5 or higher, where this bug did
not exist. I do not know how the scores above 10 million points were
obtained, I have heard there are tricks on the endgame to accomplish this,
and I am diligently trying to learn them.

NOTE:
^^^^^

The player killed in a pool of water in the endgame was not really on
the endgame. He was on a normal hell level with a moat, and the game
would not let him leave the level by any means or teleport, as though
it was the endgame. Since there were no altars and nothing more to do,
the player had to have his character commit suicide. I mention this
in case the game designers are not aware of this problem. The game
was at patchlevel 7, running on Unix on a Sun 3. The error occured when
the game was restored after being saved.
